# Window motion

Windows main and launcher windows use `shellWindowChrome`: opaque native windows, `transparent: false`, `thickFrame: true`, `roundedCorners: true`. Never restore alpha shell windows for a fixed outer radius or replace native transitions with geometry/CSS animation. Pets and overlays keep their separate transparency policy. Respect OS animation preferences.

Run `node scripts/run-window-motion-qa.mjs` on Windows after shell changes, Electron upgrades or upstream integration, alongside `npm test`. HWND styles and real IPC state checks do not replace visible transition acceptance. Update the feature card and decisions if the contract changes.

